# ESPHome 2026.10.2 native CC1101 packet-mode diagnostic patch

This patch applies only to the ESPHome built-in component
`esphome/components/cc1101/cc1101.cpp`. It does not alter this repository's
`components/rtl433` external component and must not be combined with an
`rtl433:` instance in the same firmware while the built-in `cc1101:`
component owns the transceiver.

## Apply

1. Locate ESPHome 2026.10.2's
   `esphome/components/cc1101/cc1101.cpp`.
2. Save a backup.
3. Apply the patch below to the function `CC1101Component::loop()`.
4. Compile with the existing `example-flowis-cc1101-packet-mode.yaml`,
   retaining `crc_enable: true`.

The patch:
- separates true RX FIFO overflow from an empty FIFO wake-up;
- logs the raw RXBYTES register value and GPIO4/GDO0 level;
- logs the raw variable packet length and byte count before discarding;
- logs CRC rejection separately, including RSSI, FREQEST and LQI;
- logs accepted packet metadata without changing radio settings or callback data.

It intentionally does not try to read a complete packet after a length/FIFO
state already judged invalid, and does not change sync, modem, CRC, whitening
or Manchester settings.

## Replacement function

Replace the existing `CC1101Component::loop()` implementation with:

```cpp
void CC1101Component::loop() {
  this->disable_loop();

  if (this->state_.PKT_FORMAT != static_cast<uint8_t>(PacketFormat::PACKET_FORMAT_FIFO) ||
      this->gdo0_pin_ == nullptr) {
    return;
  }

  const bool gdo0_high = this->gdo0_pin_->digital_read();
  if (!gdo0_high) {
    return;
  }

  // RXBYTES contains NUM_RXBYTES in bits 0..6 and RXFIFO_OVERFLOW in bit 7.
  this->read_(Register::RXBYTES);
  const uint8_t rxbytes_raw = this->state_.RXBYTES;
  const uint8_t rx_bytes = this->state_.NUM_RXBYTES;
  const bool overflow = this->state_.RXFIFO_OVERFLOW;

  if (overflow) {
    ESP_LOGW(TAG,
             "FLOWIS_DIAG FIFO_OVERFLOW raw=0x%02X count=%u GDO0=%u MARCSTATE=%u",
             rxbytes_raw, rx_bytes, static_cast<unsigned>(gdo0_high),
             static_cast<unsigned>(this->state_.MARC_STATE));
    this->enter_idle_();
    this->strobe_(Command::FRX);
    this->enter_rx_();
    return;
  }

  if (rx_bytes == 0) {
    ESP_LOGW(TAG,
             "FLOWIS_DIAG FIFO_EMPTY raw=0x%02X GDO0=%u MARCSTATE=%u",
             rxbytes_raw, static_cast<unsigned>(gdo0_high),
             static_cast<unsigned>(this->state_.MARC_STATE));
    this->enter_idle_();
    this->strobe_(Command::FRX);
    this->enter_rx_();
    return;
  }

  uint8_t payload_length = 0;
  uint8_t expected_rx = 0;

  if (this->state_.LENGTH_CONFIG == static_cast<uint8_t>(LengthConfig::LENGTH_CONFIG_VARIABLE)) {
    this->read_(Register::FIFO, &payload_length, 1);
    expected_rx = static_cast<uint8_t>(payload_length + 1);
  } else {
    payload_length = this->state_.PKTLEN;
    expected_rx = payload_length;
  }

  if (payload_length == 0 || payload_length > 64 || rx_bytes != expected_rx) {
    ESP_LOGW(TAG,
             "FLOWIS_DIAG INVALID_PACKET rxbytes_raw=0x%02X rx_bytes=%u "
             "length=0x%02X (%u) expected_rx=%u GDO0=%u MARCSTATE=%u",
             rxbytes_raw, rx_bytes, payload_length, payload_length, expected_rx,
             static_cast<unsigned>(gdo0_high),
             static_cast<unsigned>(this->state_.MARC_STATE));
    this->enter_idle_();
    this->strobe_(Command::FRX);
    this->enter_rx_();
    return;
  }

  this->packet_.resize(payload_length);
  this->read_(Register::FIFO, this->packet_.data(), payload_length);

  // Capture packet status registers after the FIFO has been read.
  this->read_(Register::FREQEST);
  this->read_(Register::RSSI);
  this->read_(Register::LQI);

  const float freq_offset =
      static_cast<int8_t>(this->state_.FREQEST) * (XTAL_FREQUENCY / (1 << 14));
  const float rssi = (this->state_.RSSI * RSSI_STEP) - RSSI_OFFSET;
  const bool crc_ok = (this->state_.LQI & STATUS_CRC_OK_MASK) != 0;
  const uint8_t lqi = this->state_.LQI & STATUS_LQI_MASK;

  if (this->state_.CRC_EN != 0 && !crc_ok) {
    ESP_LOGW(TAG,
             "FLOWIS_DIAG CRC_REJECT len=%u RSSI=%.1f dBm FREQEST=%+.0f Hz LQI=%u",
             static_cast<unsigned>(this->packet_.size()), rssi, freq_offset,
             static_cast<unsigned>(lqi));
  } else {
    ESP_LOGD(TAG,
             "FLOWIS_DIAG PACKET_ACCEPT len=%u CRC=%s RSSI=%.1f dBm "
             "FREQEST=%+.0f Hz LQI=%u",
             static_cast<unsigned>(this->packet_.size()),
             this->state_.CRC_EN == 0 ? "DISABLED" : "OK",
             rssi, freq_offset, static_cast<unsigned>(lqi));
    this->call_listeners_(this->packet_, freq_offset, rssi, lqi);
  }

  // Return to RX exactly as the original ESPHome implementation does.
  this->enter_idle_();
  this->strobe_(Command::FRX);
  this->enter_rx_();
}
```

## Important caveat

ESPHome's GDO0 packet-mode configuration is set to assert at FIFO threshold
or end-of-packet. This diagnostic patch makes the current driver's decision
visible; it does not yet redesign packet acquisition. If the output shows
`INVALID_PACKET` with repeated `rx_bytes=65`, or a nonsensical length byte,
the next change should be a separate, carefully tested receive-state-machine
fix in ESPHome's native CC1101 component. Do not mistake `CRC_REJECT` for a
confirmed bad over-the-air CRC if the packet was already truncated or
misaligned before reading.

## Expected useful outcomes

- `FIFO_OVERFLOW`: hardware overflow status bit was set.
- `FIFO_EMPTY`: GDO0 was high but RXBYTES reported zero; not a confirmed overflow.
- `INVALID_PACKET`: the driver's current variable-length/byte-count validation rejected the frame.
- `CRC_REJECT`: a structurally accepted packet was read, but CC1101 reported CRC failure.
- `PACKET_ACCEPT`: CC1101 delivered a packet and, with CRC enabled, the hardware CRC status passed.
